                <pb facs="ho_d12-1" n="1" xml:id="ho_d12-1"/>

                <head>HO–12. Editorial Note</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1960-04-22"
                            >April 22, 1960</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In an exchange of notes between Ambassador Robert
                        Newbegin, and Andrés Alvarado
                        Puerto, the Honduran Minister of Foreign Affairs, on April 22,
                    and May 20, 1960, respectively, the United States Government informed the
                    Republic of Honduras of its desire to amend and to extend for an additional
                    period of time beginning on March 6, 1958, the United States Army and Air Force
                    Mission agreements of March 6, 1950 (1 UST
                    199). Alvarado accepted the American proposals, and the agreement entered into
                    force on May 20, 1960, retroactive to March 6, 1958. For the texts of the notes
                    exchanged, see 11 UST (pt. 2) 1507.
                    Documentation concerning the negotiation of this agreement is in Department of
                    State files 715.58 and 611.157.</p>
            </div>
